"use strict";

module.exports = {
  slug:  "guard-content",
  title: "Guard Content",
  body: [
  "<h1>Guard Content</h1>",
  "<p>Content guards handle text-like formats that are accepted from users, generated by operators, stored in objects, or served back to clients. This page contains the full documentation for the CSV, HTML, SVG, and Markdown guards.</p>",
  "<ul>",
  "  <li><a href=\"#guard-csv\">CSV content safety</a></li>",
  "  <li><a href=\"#guard-html\">HTML content safety</a></li>",
  "  <li><a href=\"#guard-svg\">SVG content safety</a></li>",
  "  <li><a href=\"#guard-markdown\">Markdown content safety</a></li>",
  "</ul>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-csv\">CSV content safety <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-csv\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv</code> is the CSV content-safety primitive. It wraps the lower-level <code>b.csv</code> RFC 4180 parser/serializer with the broader threat catalog operators face when emitting CSVs from user-supplied data: formula injection (CWE-1236), Unicode bidi override (CVE-2021-42574 Trojan Source), C0 controls, null bytes, BOM injection, homoglyph and zero-width chars, dialect ambiguity, numeric precision loss, schema drift, CSV-bombs, and PII leakage. Composes <code>b.gateContract</code> for uniform composition with <code>b.staticServe</code> / <code>b.fileUpload</code> / <code>b.mail</code> / <code>b.objectStore</code>.</p>",
  "<p>Naming convention: <code>guard-*</code> denotes the framework's content-safety family, distinct from the <code>safe-*</code> parser family (<code>safeJson</code> / <code>safeUrl</code> / <code>safeBuffer</code> / <code>safeSql</code> / <code>safeAsync</code>) which means \"parser/validator with safer defaults.\" Every guard-* primitive ships a <code>.gate(opts)</code> factory whose return value matches the <code>b.gateContract</code> shape; host primitives consume gates uniformly via <code>contentSafety[\".csv\"]</code>-style opts.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-csv-serialize\">b.guardCsv.serialize(rows, opts?) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-csv-serialize\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                 \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\" | \"email-attachment\",",
  "  delimiter:               \",\", \";\", \"\\t\",   // default \",\"",
  "  lineEnding:              \"\\r\\n\" | \"\\n\",  // default \"\\r\\n\"",
  "  headers:                 [string] | false, // default: derived from row 0",
  "  formulaInjectionPolicy:  \"prefix-tab\" | \"prefix-quote\" | \"wrap-with-quotes-and-prefix\" | \"reject\" | \"allowlist\" | \"audit-only\",",
  "  formulasAllowlist:       [string],         // SUM/AVG/COUNT/MIN/MAX/IF/CONCATENATE by default",
  "  bomPrefix:               boolean,          // emit UTF-8 BOM at byte 0 (Excel compatibility)",
  "  maxRows:                 number,           // default: 1,048,576 rows",
  "  maxCellBytes:            number,           // default: C.BYTES.kib(64)",
  "  maxTotalBytes:           number,           // default: C.BYTES.gib(1)",
  "  maxColumns:              number,           // default: 1024",
  "  bidiCharPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlCharPolicy:       \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"allow\",",
  "  homoglyphPolicy:         \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullByteHandling:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"allow\",",
  "  trailingWhitespacePolicy: \"trim\" | \"preserve\" | \"reject\",",
  "  dialectPolicy:           \"strict\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  numericPrecisionPolicy:  \"decimal-string-above-safe-int\" | \"scientific\" | \"reject-bigint\",",
  "  piiPolicy:               \"redact\" | \"preserve\",",
  "  redact:                  b.redact,         // wired when piiPolicy: \"redact\"",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns a CSV string. Profiles bundle policy choices: <code>strict</code> wraps every formula-prefixed cell with a leading apostrophe and refuses bidi / control / null bytes; <code>balanced</code> prefixes formulas with a tab and strips bidi / control chars; <code>permissive</code> prefixes formulas and strips dangerous chars; <code>email-attachment</code> is strict + emits the UTF-8 BOM so Excel loads the file with the right encoding.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var rows = [",
  "  { id: 1, name: \"alice\",     amount: 100 },",
  "  { id: 2, name: \"=cmd|x\",    amount: 50  },   // operator-controlled cell",
  "];",
  "var safe = b.guardCsv.serialize(rows, { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → \"id,name,amount\\r\\n1,alice,100\\r\\n2,'=cmd|x,50\\r\\n\"",
  "//                                ^ leading apostrophe defangs the formula",
  "b.guardCsv.PROFILES;   // referenced for symbol-resolve gate",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-csv-validate\">b.guardCsv.validate(input, opts?) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-csv-validate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                 \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\" | \"email-attachment\",",
  "  bidiCharPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlCharPolicy:       \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"allow\",",
  "  homoglyphPolicy:         \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullByteHandling:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"allow\",",
  "  dialectPolicy:           \"strict\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  bomPrefix:               boolean,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Non-mutating threat scan. Returns <code>{ ok, issues }</code> where <code>issues</code> is an array of detected concerns (kind / severity / location / snippet / ruleId). Use this when an operator wants to inspect content before deciding what to do — the gate-shaped <code>.gate()</code> wraps validate + sanitize + decision logic into the uniform shape host primitives consume.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var rv = b.guardCsv.validate(\"hello\\u202Eevil\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// rv.ok === false",
  "// rv.issues[0].kind === \"bidi-override\"",
  "// rv.issues[0].severity === \"critical\"",
  "// rv.issues[0].ruleId === \"csv.bidi\"",
  "b.guardCsv.validate;   // referenced for symbol-resolve gate",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-csv-gate\">b.guardCsv.gate(opts?) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-csv-gate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:               \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\" | \"email-attachment\",",
  "  compliancePosture:     \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  mode:                  \"enforce\" | \"warn-only\" | \"shadow\" | \"audit-only\" | \"log-only\" | \"canary\",",
  "  audit:                 b.audit,",
  "  observability:         b.observability,",
  "  forensicSnippetBytes:  number,                 // first N bytes of refused content captured",
  "  forensicEvidenceStore: { write },               // operator-supplied vault for forensic snippets",
  "  cache:                 b.cache,                 // memoize gate decision per content hash",
  "  cacheTtlMs:            number,",
  "  maxRuntimeMs:          number,                  // default: 30s",
  "  beforeCheck, afterCheck, onIssue, onSanitize, onRefuse, onAudit,  // operator hooks",
  "  operatorRules:         [{ id, detect, severity, reason }],        // additive detection rules",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns a gate satisfying the <code>b.gateContract</code> shape. Host primitives consume it via uniform <code>contentSafety[\".csv\"]</code> opts. Compliance postures pre-set the policy bundle for HIPAA / PCI-DSS / GDPR / SOC 2 CC7 audit regimes — operators layer overrides on top.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">// Wire a strict CSV gate into b.staticServe so every served .csv is",
  "// scanned before bytes leave the framework.",
  "var csvGate = b.guardCsv.gate({",
  "  profile:               \"strict\",",
  "  compliancePosture:     \"soc2\",",
  "  forensicSnippetBytes:  256,",
  "  operatorRules: [{",
  "    id:       \"company.no-internal-domains\",",
  "    detect:   function (ctx) {",
  "      var s = ctx.bytes.toString ? ctx.bytes.toString(\"utf8\") : String(ctx.bytes);",
  "      return /\\binternal\\.corp\\.local\\b/.test(s);",
  "    },",
  "    severity: \"high\",",
  "    reason:   \"internal hostname leakage\",",
  "  }],",
  "});",
  "// var serve = b.staticServe.create({",
  "//   root: path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"exports\"),",
  "//   contentSafety: { \".csv\": csvGate },",
  "// });",
  "csvGate.metrics();   // → { passed, refused, sanitized, audited, warned, p50RuntimeMs }",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-csv-schema\">b.guardCsv.schema({ columns }) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-csv-schema\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  columns: [",
  "    { name: \"id\",    type: \"number\", min: 0 },",
  "    { name: \"email\", type: \"string\", regex: /^[^@]+@[^@]+$/ },",
  "    { name: \"ssn\",   type: \"string\", nullable: true,  pii: \"ssn\" },",
  "    { name: \"amt\",   type: \"number\", nullable: false, max: 1e6 },",
  "  ],",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Typed serializer. Validates every cell against the column type / regex / range / nullable rule before emit; throws on schema drift. Use this when emitting CSVs from a typed source (database query rows, audit-log exports) so a schema change downstream surfaces as an explicit error rather than silent corruption.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var emitter = b.guardCsv.schema({",
  "  columns: [",
  "    { name: \"id\",   type: \"number\" },",
  "    { name: \"name\", type: \"string\" },",
  "  ],",
  "});",
  "var out = emitter.serialize([",
  "  { id: 1, name: \"alice\" },",
  "  { id: 2, name: \"bob\" },",
  "]);",
  "emitter.validate;   // referenced for symbol-resolve gate",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html\">HTML content safety <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml</code> is the HTML content-safety primitive. It implements the framework's detection + sanitization layer for the XSS / DOM-clobbering / mXSS / dangerous-tag / event-handler / dangerous-URL-scheme / CSS-injection threat catalog grounded in current sanitizer research (DOMPurify CVE series, OWASP XSS / DOM-Clobbering / HTML5 Security cheat sheets, PortSwigger and Sonar mXSS write-ups, html5sec.org). Composes <code>b.gateContract</code> for uniform composition with <code>b.staticServe</code> / <code>b.fileUpload</code> / <code>b.mail</code>. Auto-registers into <code>b.guardAll</code>.</p>",
  "<p><strong>Operator-facing trade-off:</strong> for hostile sources, <code>validate + reject</code> is the strong path. The token-level <code>sanitize</code> handles the common cases (strip dangerous tags + their executable bodies, strip on* attributes, strip dangerous URL schemes, strip CSS injection patterns, drop comments, drop doctypes, drop CDATA) but no non-DOM HTML sanitizer can claim immunity from mXSS — display untrusted HTML under a strict CSP (default-src 'none' or sandboxed iframe) regardless.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-validate\">b.guardHtml.validate(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-validate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                 \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",  // default \"strict\"",
  "  compliancePosture:       \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  // ---- whole-input policies (override profile) ----",
  "  bidiPolicy:              \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:           \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  zeroWidthPolicy:         \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  cssPolicy:               \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  domClobberPolicy:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  mxssHintPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  // ---- tag / attr / url policy ----",
  "  allowedTags:             string[],            // overrides profile",
  "  allowedAttrs:            string[],            // overrides profile",
  "  urlSchemes:              string[],            // additive allowlist",
  "  allowImageData:          boolean,             // permit data:image/* on <img>",
  "  allowComments:           boolean,             // pass HTML comments through sanitize",
  "  // ---- size caps (DoS-shape) ----",
  "  maxBytes:                number,              // total document size",
  "  maxAttrValueBytes:       number,              // per-attribute value cap",
  "  maxTagDepth:             number,              // nesting depth",
  "  maxAttrsPerTag:          number,              // attributes per element",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns <code>{ ok, issues }</code>. Each issue is <code>{ kind, severity, ruleId, location, snippet }</code>. <code>ok=false</code> when any issue has severity <code>critical</code> or <code>high</code>.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var rv = b.guardHtml.validate(\"<p>hello</p>\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "rv.ok;        // true",
  "var hostile = b.guardHtml.validate('<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>', { profile: \"balanced\" });",
  "hostile.ok;   // false — issue kind \"event-handler\"",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-sanitize\">b.guardHtml.sanitize(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-sanitize\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:           \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",  // default \"strict\"",
  "  allowedTags:       string[],",
  "  allowedAttrs:      string[],",
  "  urlSchemes:        string[],",
  "  allowImageData:    boolean,",
  "  allowComments:     boolean,",
  "  bidiPolicy:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:     \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:    \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  zeroWidthPolicy:   \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns the sanitized HTML string. Strips dangerous tags AND their text content (script/style/iframe/object/embed/applet/template/svg/math etc. — body parsed as code in the host). Strips every <code>on*</code> attribute family-wide. Strips dangerous URL schemes per <code>urlSchemes</code>. Strips style-attribute CSS injection tokens. Strips DOM-clobbering <code>id</code> / <code>name</code> values matching the framework's denylist of well-known JS globals. Drops doctype, CDATA, and comments unless <code>allowComments=true</code>.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">b.guardHtml.sanitize('<script>alert(1)</script><p>hi <b>there</b></p>',",
  "                    { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → \"<p>hi <b>there</b></p>\"",
  "",
  "b.guardHtml.sanitize('<a href=\"javascript:alert(1)\">click</a><a href=\"https://ok\">ok</a>',",
  "                    { profile: \"balanced\" });",
  "// → drops the javascript: href, keeps the https one",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-escape\">b.guardHtml.escapeText(value) / b.guardHtml.escapeAttr(value) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-escape\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p>Always-correct entity escapers for embedding values into HTML text-content or attribute-value contexts respectively. <code>escapeText</code> handles <code>&amp;</code> <code>&lt;</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>&quot;</code> <code>&#39;</code>; <code>escapeAttr</code> additionally encodes <code>&#96;</code> (legacy IE attribute terminator) and <code>&#61;</code> (unquoted-attribute edge case). null / undefined input returns the empty string.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">b.guardHtml.escapeText(\"<oops>&amp;\");   // &lt;oops&gt;&amp;amp;",
  "b.guardHtml.escapeAttr('a\"b');          // a&quot;b",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-gate\">b.guardHtml.gate(opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-gate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:               \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",  // default \"strict\"",
  "  compliancePosture:     \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  mode:                  \"enforce\" | \"warn-only\" | \"shadow\" | \"audit-only\" | \"log-only\" | \"canary\",",
  "  audit:                 b.audit,                          // emits guardHtml.gate.* events",
  "  observability:         b.observability,",
  "  forensicEvidenceStore: { put }, forensicSnippetBytes: number,",
  "  cache:                 b.cache, cacheTtlMs: number,",
  "  maxRuntimeMs:          number,",
  "  beforeCheck/afterCheck/onIssue/onSanitize/onRefuse/onAudit: hooks,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns a <code>b.gateContract</code>-shaped gate. Composes into <code>b.staticServe.create({ contentSafety: { \".html\": gate } })</code>, <code>b.fileUpload.create({ contentSafety: gate })</code>, and any host primitive that takes a gate. Auto-registered into <code>b.guardAll</code> — most operators reach for <code>b.guardAll.byExtension({ profile: \"strict\" })</code> which wires every guard at once.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var htmlGate = b.guardHtml.gate({",
  "  profile:       \"strict\",",
  "  audit:         b.audit,",
  "  observability: b.observability,",
  "});",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-threat-catalog\">Threat catalog <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-threat-catalog\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p>Every threat in the family is detected (returns an issue) and where applicable, sanitized:</p>",
  "<ul>",
  "<li><strong>Dangerous tags</strong> — script, style, link, meta, base, iframe, object, embed, applet, form, input, button, frame, frameset, marquee, blink, plaintext, xmp, audio, video, source, track, math, svg, template, noscript, noembed, noframes, portal, dialog, keygen, menuitem.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Event-handler attributes</strong> — every attribute matching <code>/^on[a-z]/</code> denied. Catches the entire HTML5 event-handler family without a manual list that rots when WHATWG specs a new event.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Form-override attributes</strong> — formaction / formmethod / formenctype / formtarget / formnovalidate (CWE-1021).</li>",
  "<li><strong>Iframe inline-HTML</strong> — srcdoc denied unconditionally.</li>",
  "<li><strong>CSP-bypass-shaped attributes</strong> — nonce, integrity, crossorigin stripped (operator-controlled only).</li>",
  "<li><strong>URL scheme allowlist</strong> — http / https / mailto / tel always; <code>data:image/*</code> allowed on <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> when <code>allowImageData</code> set; javascript / vbscript / livescript / mocha / data (outside image context) / file / mhtml / jar / intent / view-source / feed always denied. Entity-encoded schemes (<code>&amp;#x6A;avascript:...</code>) detected after entity decode.</li>",
  "<li><strong>CSS injection</strong> — <code>expression(</code> (IE), <code>behavior:</code> (IE), <code>-moz-binding</code> (Firefox legacy), <code>javascript:</code> / <code>vbscript:</code> inside <code>url()</code>, <code>@import</code> / <code>@namespace</code>.</li>",
  "<li><strong>DOM clobbering</strong> — id / name attributes matching the framework's denylist of well-known JS globals (<code>document</code>, <code>cookie</code>, <code>__proto__</code>, <code>constructor</code>, <code>innerHTML</code>, <code>src</code>, <code>href</code>, ...) on form / input / button / a / img / iframe / object elements.</li>",
  "<li><strong>mXSS hints</strong> — <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;math&gt;</code> namespace-context-shift parents flagged; refused under strict, audited under balanced.</li>",
  "<li><strong>IE conditional comments</strong> — <code>&lt;!--[if ...]&gt;...&lt;![endif]--&gt;</code> denied (legacy IE rendering executable script vector).</li>",
  "<li><strong>Unicode bidi override</strong> (CVE-2021-42574 Trojan Source), C0 control chars, null bytes, zero-width chars — same codepoint catalog as <code>b.guardCsv</code>; threat-detection regex literals composed programmatically from numeric codepoint range tables.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Anti-DoS caps</strong> — total-document size, per-attribute-value size, max-tag-depth (prevents recursion-shape parsers from stack-blowing), max-attribute-count-per-tag.</li>",
  "</ul>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-profiles\">Profiles <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-profiles\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>strict</strong> — minimal text-formatting allowlist (p, br, hr, b, i, u, em, strong, code, pre, h1–h6, ul, ol, li, blockquote, span, div). Allowed attrs: class, title, lang, dir. URL schemes: http, https, mailto, tel. <code>allowImageData=false</code>. Reject every dangerous policy class. 2 MiB document cap.</p>",
  "<p><strong>balanced</strong> — adds links, images, tables, semantic markup. Allowed URL schemes adds ftp. <code>allowImageData=true</code>. Strip rather than reject for character-class threats (bidi / control / null / zero-width). 8 MiB document cap.</p>",
  "<p><strong>permissive</strong> — every tag NOT in the dangerous-tags denylist. Adds tabindex / accesskey to allowed attrs. Adds ftp / sftp / ws / wss schemes. Bidi and CSS injection audit-only. 32 MiB document cap.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-html-compliance\">Compliance postures <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-html-compliance\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>hipaa</strong> / <strong>pci-dss</strong> / <strong>soc2</strong> — strict allowlist + reject on every threat class + forensic snapshot capture (256-byte snippet, 512 for soc2). pci-dss additionally locks the URL allowlist to http / https / mailto / tel.</p>",
  "<p><strong>gdpr</strong> — balanced allowlist + strip rather than reject (operator can serve sanitized output) + 128-byte forensic snapshots.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg\">SVG content safety <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardSvg</code> is the SVG content-safety primitive. SVG's broad attack surface (XML namespace, JavaScript via <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>, HTML escape via <code>&lt;foreignObject&gt;</code>, dynamic attribute targeting via animation elements, XML entity expansion, SVGZ compression, SSRF via cross-origin <code>&lt;use&gt;</code>) makes it one of the highest-risk image-shaped formats to accept on uploads. Threat catalog grounded in current research (Fortinet anatomy of SVG attack surface, Angular GHSA-jrmj-c5cx-3cw6 + GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49, SVGO CVE-2026-29074 billion-laughs DoS, siyuan-note GHSA-5hc8-qmg8-pw27 animate-element bypass, cure53/DOMPurify issue #233 xlink:href filtering). Auto-registers into <code>b.guardAll</code>.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-validate\">b.guardSvg.validate(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-validate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                 \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  compliancePosture:       \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  bidiPolicy:              \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:           \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  zeroWidthPolicy:         \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  cssPolicy:               \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  doctypePolicy:           \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  cdataPolicy:             \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  processingInstrPolicy:   \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  svgzPolicy:              \"reject\",",
  "  allowedTags:             string[],",
  "  allowedAttrs:            string[],",
  "  urlSchemes:              string[],",
  "  allowImageData:          boolean,",
  "  allowExternalRefs:       boolean,         // false = same-origin / fragment refs only",
  "  allowAnimation:          boolean,         // gates animate / set / animateMotion / animateTransform",
  "  allowedAttrNames:        string[],        // safe attributeName targets for animation elements",
  "  maxBytes:                number,",
  "  maxAttrValueBytes:       number,",
  "  maxElementCount:         number,         // anti-billion-laughs DoS cap",
  "  maxUseDepth:             number,         // <use> nesting cap",
  "  maxAttrsPerTag:          number,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns <code>{ ok, issues }</code>. Issue kinds: <code>svgz-compressed</code>, <code>doctype</code>, <code>entity-declaration</code>, <code>cdata</code>, <code>processing-instruction</code>, <code>dangerous-tag</code>, <code>animation-target</code>, <code>event-handler</code>, <code>dangerous-url-scheme</code>, <code>external-ref</code>, <code>css-injection</code>, <code>bidi-override</code>, <code>null-byte</code>, <code>control-char</code>, <code>use-depth-cap</code>, <code>element-count-cap</code>, <code>attr-count-cap</code>, <code>attr-value-too-large</code>.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">// Hostile: animate-element href hijack (recent CVE class).",
  "var rv = b.guardSvg.validate(",
  "  '<svg><animate attributeName=\"href\" to=\"javascript:alert(1)\"/></svg>',",
  "  { profile: \"permissive\" });",
  "rv.ok;       // false — animation-target issue: animation attributeName=\"href\" can rewrite parent's href",
  "",
  "// Hostile: SVGZ compressed payload (gzip magic 0x1F 0x8B).",
  "var rv2 = b.guardSvg.validate(Buffer.from([0x1F, 0x8B, 0x08]), { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "rv2.ok;      // false — svgz-compressed; operator must ungzip before validating",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-sanitize\">b.guardSvg.sanitize(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-sanitize\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                 \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  allowedTags:             string[],",
  "  allowedAttrs:            string[],",
  "  urlSchemes:              string[],",
  "  allowImageData:          boolean,",
  "  allowExternalRefs:       boolean,",
  "  allowAnimation:          boolean,",
  "  allowedAttrNames:        string[],",
  "  bidiPolicy:              \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:           \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns the sanitized SVG string. Strips dangerous tags AND their text content (script / foreignObject / handler / iframe / embed / object body parsed as code in the host parser). Strips every <code>on*</code> attribute family-wide. Strips dangerous URL schemes per <code>urlSchemes</code>. Strips cross-origin <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;feImage&gt;</code> external refs unless <code>allowExternalRefs=true</code>. Strips style-attribute CSS injection tokens. Strips animation elements whose <code>attributeName</code> targets an unsafe attribute (href / xlink:href / src). Throws on SVGZ input — operator must ungzip first.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">b.guardSvg.sanitize(",
  "  '<svg><script>alert(1)</script><circle r=\"10\"/></svg>',",
  "  { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → \"<svg><circle r=\\\"10\\\"/></svg>\" — script tag + body dropped",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-gate\">b.guardSvg.gate(opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-gate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:               \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  compliancePosture:     \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  mode:                  \"enforce\" | \"warn-only\" | \"shadow\" | \"audit-only\" | \"log-only\" | \"canary\",",
  "  audit:                 b.audit,",
  "  observability:         b.observability,",
  "  forensicEvidenceStore: { put }, forensicSnippetBytes: number,",
  "  cache:                 b.cache, cacheTtlMs: number,",
  "  maxRuntimeMs:          number,",
  "  beforeCheck/afterCheck/onIssue/onSanitize/onRefuse/onAudit: hooks,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns a <code>b.gateContract</code>-shaped gate. SVGZ payloads always refuse — the gate cannot peer inside compressed content; operators that need SVGZ ungzip first then re-gate the inner SVG.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var svgGate = b.guardSvg.gate({",
  "  profile:       \"strict\",",
  "  audit:         b.audit,",
  "  observability: b.observability,",
  "});",
  "// Compose into staticServe content-safety:",
  "// b.staticServe.create({ contentSafety: { \".svg\": svgGate } });",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-threat-catalog\">Threat catalog <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-threat-catalog\">#</a></h2>",
  "<ul>",
  "<li><strong>Dangerous SVG tags</strong> — script, foreignObject (HTML namespace escape hatch), handler, listener, iframe, embed, object, audio, video. Refused or stripped per profile.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Animation elements</strong> — animate, set, animateMotion, animateTransform — recent CVE class where attributeName retroactively rewrites a parent element's attribute. SMIL animation attributeName allowlist limits targets to safe visual properties (cx, cy, r, x, y, width, height, fill, stroke, opacity, transform, ...). attributeName=\"href\" or attributeName=\"xlink:href\" with values=\"javascript:alert(1)\" is the published bypass shape; refused.</li>",
  "<li><strong>on* / SMIL event-handler attributes</strong> — every attribute matching <code>/^on[a-z]/</code> denied. Includes SMIL onbegin / onend / onrepeat.</li>",
  "<li><strong>href / xlink:href dangerous URL schemes</strong> — javascript / vbscript / data (outside image context) / file / mhtml / view-source / feed denied. Entity-encoded scheme bypasses (<code>&amp;#x6A;avascript:</code>) decoded before scheme check.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Cross-origin <code>&lt;use&gt;</code></strong> — same-origin (relative paths, fragment-only #id) allowed under strict; absolute URLs with scheme refused (SSRF + XSS chain).</li>",
  "<li><strong>XML DOCTYPE declarations</strong> — refused unconditionally regardless of profile. Catches billion-laughs entity expansion (CVE-2026-29074 SVGO class), external entity loading (XXE), SYSTEM identifier exfiltration.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Custom entity declarations</strong> — <code>&lt;!ENTITY ...&gt;</code> inside the SVG stream refused.</li>",
  "<li><strong>CDATA + processing instructions</strong> — refused or audited per profile (often used to hide payloads from naive scanners; <code>&lt;?xml-stylesheet ... ?&gt;</code> is a CSS injection vector).</li>",
  "<li><strong>SVGZ compressed payloads</strong> — magic bytes 0x1F 0x8B refused at gate level. Operator must ungzip and re-gate the inner SVG.</li>",
  "<li><strong>CSS injection in style attribute</strong> — same vocabulary as guard-html (expression / behavior / -moz-binding / javascript: in url() / @import / @namespace).</li>",
  "<li><strong>&lt;use&gt;-recursion DoS</strong> — caps via maxUseDepth + maxElementCount.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Unicode bidi (CVE-2021-42574 Trojan Source) / C0 control chars / null bytes / zero-width</strong> — same codepoint catalog as guard-csv / guard-html.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Anti-DoS caps</strong> — total-document size, element count (defence against entity-free DoS via repeated literal expansion), use-element nesting depth, attribute-count-per-element, per-attribute-value size.</li>",
  "</ul>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-profiles\">Profiles <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-profiles\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>strict</strong> — minimal text + shapes (svg, g, defs, title, desc, metadata, path, rect, circle, ellipse, line, polyline, polygon, text, tspan, textpath). No animation. No external refs. 2 MiB document cap. Element count 8192. Use-depth 8.</p>",
  "<p><strong>balanced</strong> — adds <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;symbol&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;image&gt;</code> with same-origin or http(s), gradients, filters, masks, <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>. allowExternalRefs=true. 8 MiB document cap. Element count 65536.</p>",
  "<p><strong>permissive</strong> — adds animation elements (with strict attributeName allowlist still enforced). 32 MiB document cap. Element count 262144.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-svg-compliance\">Compliance postures <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-svg-compliance\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>hipaa</strong> / <strong>pci-dss</strong> / <strong>soc2</strong> — strict allowlist + reject every threat class + forensic snapshots. pci-dss locks URL allowlist to http / https / mailto / tel.</p>",
  "<p><strong>gdpr</strong> — balanced allowlist + strip rather than reject. 128-byte forensic snapshots.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown\">Markdown content safety <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardMarkdown</code> is the markdown content-safety primitive. Threat catalog grounded in current research: CVE-2026-30838 CommonMark DisallowedRawHtml whitespace-tag bypass; CVE-2025-9540 Markup Markdown javascript: link XSS; CVE-2025-7969 markdown-it ReDoS; CVE-2025-6493 CodeMirror Markdown catastrophic backtracking; CVE-2025-24981 MDC autolink XSS; CVE-2026-33500 AVideo Parsedown link bypass; GHSA-gwjh-c548-f787 NuGetGallery autolink XSS; Joplin GHSA-hff8-hjwv-j9q7 RCE via untrusted markdown link. Auto-registers into <code>b.guardAll</code>. Source-level scan — runs BEFORE any downstream renderer (marked / markdown-it / commonmark / remark / parsedown) sees the input.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-validate\">b.guardMarkdown.validate(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-validate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  compliancePosture:      \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  rawHtmlPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  dangerousTagPolicy:     \"reject\" | \"allow\",            // refused at every profile",
  "  dangerousSchemePolicy:  \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",  // refused at every profile",
  "  autolinkSchemePolicy:   \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  referenceLinkPolicy:    \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  imageSchemePolicy:      \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  htmlCommentPolicy:      \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  frontMatterPolicy:      \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  codeFenceLangPolicy:    \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  doctypePolicy:          \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  emphasisRunPolicy:      \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  filePolicy:             \"reject\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  bidiPolicy:             \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:         \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  zeroWidthPolicy:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  maxBytes:               number,",
  "  maxLines:               number,",
  "  maxLinks:               number,",
  "  maxImages:              number,",
  "  maxAutolinks:           number,",
  "  maxRefDefs:             number,",
  "  maxListDepth:           number,",
  "  maxBlockquoteDepth:     number,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns <code>{ ok, issues }</code>. Issue kinds: <code>raw-html</code>, <code>dangerous-tag</code>, <code>link-scheme</code>, <code>image-scheme</code>, <code>autolink-scheme</code>, <code>reference-link-scheme</code>, <code>html-comment</code>, <code>front-matter</code>, <code>code-fence-lang</code>, <code>doctype</code>, <code>emphasis-run</code>, <code>line-cap</code>, <code>link-cap</code>, <code>image-cap</code>, <code>autolink-cap</code>, <code>ref-def-cap</code>, <code>list-depth-cap</code>, <code>blockquote-depth-cap</code>, <code>bidi-override</code>, <code>null-byte</code>, <code>control-char</code>, <code>too-large</code>.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">b.guardMarkdown.validate(\"# Title\\n\\nA [link](https://example.com).\\n\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → { ok: true, issues: [] }",
  "",
  "// Hostile: javascript: URL scheme in link (CVE-2025-9540 class).",
  "b.guardMarkdown.validate(\"[click](javascript:alert(1))\\n\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → ok=false; issues include link-scheme",
  "",
  "// Hostile: whitespace-tolerant tag bypass (CVE-2026-30838).",
  "b.guardMarkdown.validate(\"&lt;script\\n&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;\\n\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → ok=false; issues include dangerous-tag",
  "",
  "// Hostile: HTML-entity encoded scheme bypass.",
  "b.guardMarkdown.validate(\"[x](&amp;#x6A;avascript:alert(1))\\n\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "// → ok=false; the entity decoder catches the bypass before scheme match",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-sanitize\">b.guardMarkdown.sanitize(input, opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-sanitize\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:                \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  bidiPolicy:             \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  controlPolicy:          \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  nullBytePolicy:         \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "  zeroWidthPolicy:        \"reject\" | \"strip\" | \"audit\" | \"allow\",",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Strips character-class threats per policy but ALWAYS THROWS on critical (dangerous tags / dangerous URL schemes / DOCTYPE / code-fence language injection / image scheme bypass / autolink scheme bypass) — these have no safe sanitization in markdown; the only correct response is reject. Returns the cleaned markdown string when no critical threats are present.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">// Throws — no safe sanitization for javascript: URL.",
  "try { b.guardMarkdown.sanitize(\"[x](javascript:alert(1))\\n\", { profile: \"balanced\" }); }",
  "catch (e) { e.code; }   // \"markdown.link-scheme\"",
  "</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-gate\">b.guardMarkdown.gate(opts) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-gate\">#</a></h2>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">{",
  "  profile:               \"strict\" | \"balanced\" | \"permissive\",",
  "  compliancePosture:     \"hipaa\" | \"pci-dss\" | \"gdpr\" | \"soc2\",",
  "  mode:                  \"enforce\" | \"warn-only\" | \"shadow\" | \"audit-only\" | \"log-only\" | \"canary\",",
  "  audit:                 b.audit,",
  "  observability:         b.observability,",
  "  forensicEvidenceStore: { put }, forensicSnippetBytes: number,",
  "  cache:                 b.cache, cacheTtlMs: number,",
  "  maxRuntimeMs:          number,",
  "  beforeCheck/afterCheck/onIssue/onSanitize/onRefuse/onAudit: hooks,",
  "}</code></pre>",
  "<p>Returns a <code>b.gateContract</code>-shaped gate. Auto-routed via <code>b.guardAll</code> when Content-Type is <code>text/markdown</code> / <code>text/x-markdown</code> / <code>text/x-gfm</code>. Wired by default into <code>b.fileUpload</code> + <code>b.staticServe</code> at strict profile.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var mdGate = b.guardMarkdown.gate({ profile: \"strict\", audit: b.audit });</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-threat-catalog\">Threat catalog <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-threat-catalog\">#</a></h2>",
  "<ul>",
  "<li><strong>Dangerous tags</strong> (script / iframe / object / embed / form / input / meta / link / base / svg / math / video / audio / style / template / portal / marquee / etc.) — refused at every profile (script-tag class is universal). Whitespace-tolerant matching closes CVE-2026-30838 (CommonMark DisallowedRawHtml bypass via <code>&lt;script\\n&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;script\\t&gt;</code>).</li>",
  "<li><strong>Dangerous URL schemes</strong> in inline links / images / autolinks / reference-link definitions (<code>javascript:</code>, <code>vbscript:</code>, <code>livescript:</code>, <code>mocha:</code>, <code>view-source:</code>, <code>data:</code>, <code>jar:</code>, <code>blob:</code>, <code>feed:</code>, <code>tel:</code>, <code>facetime:</code>) — refused at every profile.</li>",
  "<li><strong>HTML-entity scheme bypass</strong> — <code>&amp;#x6A;avascript:</code> / <code>&amp;#106;avascript:</code> decode to <code>javascript:</code>. The gate decodes HTML entities BEFORE scheme matching (CVE-2025-24981 / Joplin GHSA-hff8-hjwv-j9q7 class).</li>",
  "<li><strong>Reference-link smuggling</strong> — <code>[text][ref]</code> paired with <code>[ref]: javascript:alert(1)</code> elsewhere in the document. The gate scans every <code>[label]: url</code> definition for dangerous schemes.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Autolink scheme bypass</strong> — <code>&lt;javascript:alert(1)&gt;</code> renders as a clickable link in many markdown engines. CVE-2025-24981 / NuGetGallery GHSA-gwjh-c548-f787 / CVE-2026-33500 Parsedown class.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Front-matter</strong> — leading <code>---\\n...\\n---</code> YAML or <code>+++\\n...\\n+++</code> TOML block. Some renderers parse the block as data; payload class equals guardYaml.</li>",
  "<li><strong>HTML comments</strong> — <code>&lt;!-- ... --&gt;</code> blocks; payload-smuggling vector (some renderers strip comments naively, others propagate).</li>",
  "<li><strong>Code-fence language injection</strong> — <code>```\"&gt;&lt;script&gt;</code> exploits renderers that paste the language tag into a class attribute without escaping. The gate refuses any language tag containing <code>&lt;</code> / <code>&gt;</code> / <code>\"</code> / <code>'</code> / <code>`</code>.</li>",
  "<li><strong>DOCTYPE inline</strong> — <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> in markdown source; XXE-shaped class if the rendered HTML is fed to an XML processor.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Catastrophic emphasis runs</strong> (CVE-2025-6493 CodeMirror class) — long runs of <code>*</code> / <code>_</code> trigger ReDoS in several markdown engines.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Anti-DoS caps</strong> — total bytes, line count, link count, image count, autolink count, reference-def count, list nesting depth, blockquote nesting depth.</li>",
  "<li><strong>Bidi / null / control / zero-width</strong> chars in text + URLs — same codepoint catalog as guard-csv/html/svg/json/yaml/xml.</li>",
  "</ul>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-profiles\">Profiles <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-profiles\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>strict</strong> — refuse every threat (raw HTML / dangerous tags / dangerous schemes / autolink schemes / reference-link smuggling / image schemes / HTML comments / front-matter / code-fence injection / DOCTYPE / catastrophic emphasis / bidi / null / control); 1 MiB cap; 4096 lines; 256 links; 128 images; depth caps 16.</p>",
  "<p><strong>balanced</strong> — dangerous tags + schemes + image schemes + autolink schemes still refused (universal); audit raw HTML / reference-links / HTML comments / front-matter / code-fence / catastrophic emphasis; strip char-class threats; 8 MiB cap; depth caps 64.</p>",
  "<p><strong>permissive</strong> — dangerous tags + dangerous schemes still refused (script-tag and javascript: are always universal); raw HTML / reference-links / HTML comments / front-matter all allowed; 64 MiB cap; depth caps 256.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-compliance\">Compliance postures <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-compliance\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><strong>hipaa</strong> / <strong>pci-dss</strong> / <strong>soc2</strong> — strict overlay + forensic snapshots (256 / 256 / 512 bytes).</p>",
  "<p><strong>gdpr</strong> — balanced overlay + 128-byte forensic snippets.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-markdown-composition\">Composition <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-markdown-composition\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p>For sites that render user-submitted markdown to HTML, layer this primitive WITH <code>b.guardHtml</code> (run guardMarkdown on the source, render via your markdown engine, run guardHtml on the rendered output). Source-level + rendered-level scans together close the residual bypass surface that either alone misses.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"guard-helper-surface\">Shared helper surface <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#guard-helper-surface\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p>Every guard in this category also exposes the shared helper surface used by operators and by <code>b.guardAll</code>: profile composition, compliance posture lookup, and local rule-pack registration.</p>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-build-profile\">b.guardCsv.buildProfile(profileOptions) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-build-profile\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.buildProfile</code> composes one of the guard's named profiles with additional operator extensions, overrides, and removals. Use it when a deployment wants to inspect the exact policy object that will feed validation or gate creation before wiring it into a host primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var profile = b.guardCsv.buildProfile({",
  "  baseProfile: \"strict\",",
  "  overrides: { mode: \"enforce\" },",
  "});",
  "typeof profile; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-compliance-posture\">b.guardCsv.compliancePosture(name) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-compliance-posture\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.compliancePosture</code> returns the guard-specific policy overlay for a named posture such as <code>soc2</code>, <code>gdpr</code>, <code>hipaa</code>, or <code>pci-dss</code>. Unknown posture names fail immediately so compliance wiring cannot silently fall back to a weaker profile.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var posture = b.guardCsv.compliancePosture(\"soc2\");",
  "typeof posture; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-load-rule-pack\">b.guardCsv.loadRulePack(pack) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-load-rule-pack\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.loadRulePack</code> registers an operator rule pack for this guard and returns the accepted pack. Rule packs give deployments a stable place to add local detection rules without forking the framework primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var pack = b.guardCsv.loadRulePack({",
  "  id: \"docs-csv-rule-pack\",",
  "  rules: [],",
  "});",
  "pack.id; // \"docs-csv-rule-pack\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"html-build-profile\">b.guardHtml.buildProfile(profileOptions) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#html-build-profile\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml.buildProfile</code> composes one of the guard's named profiles with additional operator extensions, overrides, and removals. Use it when a deployment wants to inspect the exact policy object that will feed validation or gate creation before wiring it into a host primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var profile = b.guardHtml.buildProfile({",
  "  baseProfile: \"strict\",",
  "  overrides: { mode: \"enforce\" },",
  "});",
  "typeof profile; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"html-compliance-posture\">b.guardHtml.compliancePosture(name) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#html-compliance-posture\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml.compliancePosture</code> returns the guard-specific policy overlay for a named posture such as <code>soc2</code>, <code>gdpr</code>, <code>hipaa</code>, or <code>pci-dss</code>. Unknown posture names fail immediately so compliance wiring cannot silently fall back to a weaker profile.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var posture = b.guardHtml.compliancePosture(\"soc2\");",
  "typeof posture; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"html-load-rule-pack\">b.guardHtml.loadRulePack(pack) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#html-load-rule-pack\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml.loadRulePack</code> registers an operator rule pack for this guard and returns the accepted pack. Rule packs give deployments a stable place to add local detection rules without forking the framework primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var pack = b.guardHtml.loadRulePack({",
  "  id: \"docs-html-rule-pack\",",
  "  rules: [],",
  "});",
  "pack.id; // \"docs-html-rule-pack\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"svg-build-profile\">b.guardSvg.buildProfile(profileOptions) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#svg-build-profile\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardSvg.buildProfile</code> composes one of the guard's named profiles with additional operator extensions, overrides, and removals. Use it when a deployment wants to inspect the exact policy object that will feed validation or gate creation before wiring it into a host primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var profile = b.guardSvg.buildProfile({",
  "  baseProfile: \"strict\",",
  "  overrides: { mode: \"enforce\" },",
  "});",
  "typeof profile; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"svg-compliance-posture\">b.guardSvg.compliancePosture(name) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#svg-compliance-posture\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardSvg.compliancePosture</code> returns the guard-specific policy overlay for a named posture such as <code>soc2</code>, <code>gdpr</code>, <code>hipaa</code>, or <code>pci-dss</code>. Unknown posture names fail immediately so compliance wiring cannot silently fall back to a weaker profile.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var posture = b.guardSvg.compliancePosture(\"soc2\");",
  "typeof posture; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"svg-load-rule-pack\">b.guardSvg.loadRulePack(pack) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#svg-load-rule-pack\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardSvg.loadRulePack</code> registers an operator rule pack for this guard and returns the accepted pack. Rule packs give deployments a stable place to add local detection rules without forking the framework primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var pack = b.guardSvg.loadRulePack({",
  "  id: \"docs-svg-rule-pack\",",
  "  rules: [],",
  "});",
  "pack.id; // \"docs-svg-rule-pack\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"markdown-build-profile\">b.guardMarkdown.buildProfile(profileOptions) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#markdown-build-profile\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardMarkdown.buildProfile</code> composes one of the guard's named profiles with additional operator extensions, overrides, and removals. Use it when a deployment wants to inspect the exact policy object that will feed validation or gate creation before wiring it into a host primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var profile = b.guardMarkdown.buildProfile({",
  "  baseProfile: \"strict\",",
  "  overrides: { mode: \"enforce\" },",
  "});",
  "typeof profile; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"markdown-compliance-posture\">b.guardMarkdown.compliancePosture(name) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#markdown-compliance-posture\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardMarkdown.compliancePosture</code> returns the guard-specific policy overlay for a named posture such as <code>soc2</code>, <code>gdpr</code>, <code>hipaa</code>, or <code>pci-dss</code>. Unknown posture names fail immediately so compliance wiring cannot silently fall back to a weaker profile.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var posture = b.guardMarkdown.compliancePosture(\"soc2\");",
  "typeof posture; // \"object\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"markdown-load-rule-pack\">b.guardMarkdown.loadRulePack(pack) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#markdown-load-rule-pack\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardMarkdown.loadRulePack</code> registers an operator rule pack for this guard and returns the accepted pack. Rule packs give deployments a stable place to add local detection rules without forking the framework primitive.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var pack = b.guardMarkdown.loadRulePack({",
  "  id: \"docs-markdown-rule-pack\",",
  "  rules: [],",
  "});",
  "pack.id; // \"docs-markdown-rule-pack\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-detect\">b.guardCsv.detect(input) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-detect\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.detect</code> inspects CSV source for dialect signals such as delimiter, line ending, header likelihood, encoding, and confidence. Use it for import tooling that wants to explain what the guard inferred before applying stricter validation or sanitization.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var detected = b.guardCsv.detect(\"name,amount\\r\\nalice,10\");",
  "typeof detected.confidence; // \"number\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-escape-cell\">b.guardCsv.escapeCell(value, options) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-escape-cell\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.escapeCell</code> escapes one CSV cell according to the guard policy, including formula-prefix handling. It is the low-level helper behind guarded CSV serialization when an operator needs to transform one value at a time.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var cell = b.guardCsv.escapeCell(\"=cmd\", { profile: \"strict\" });",
  "typeof cell; // \"string\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"csv-sanitize\">b.guardCsv.sanitize(input, options) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#csv-sanitize\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardCsv.sanitize</code> rewrites CSV content where the selected profile permits safe repair, then throws when the remaining issues cannot be repaired. Use it only when the caller wants a cleaned CSV string rather than a non-mutating validation report.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var csv = b.guardCsv.sanitize(\"name\\r\\nalice\", { profile: \"balanced\" });",
  "typeof csv; // \"string\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"html-escape-attr\">b.guardHtml.escapeAttr(value) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#html-escape-attr\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml.escapeAttr</code> escapes text for safe placement inside HTML attributes, including quote, backtick, and equals handling for legacy unquoted-attribute edges. Use it for hand-authored fragments that cannot be routed through a full template renderer.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var attr = b.guardHtml.escapeAttr('say \"hi\" & stay');",
  "typeof attr; // \"string\"</code></pre>",
  "<h2 id=\"html-wcag\">b.guardHtml.wcag.audit(html, options) <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#html-wcag\">#</a></h2>",
  "<p><code>b.guardHtml.wcag</code> exposes audit-only WCAG helpers under the HTML guard. It reports accessibility findings without rewriting the document, so operators can run accessibility checks alongside content-safety checks without changing output.</p>",
  "<pre><code class=\"language-javascript\">var audit = b.guardHtml.wcag.audit(\"<img>\", {});",
  "Array.isArray(audit.findings); // true</code></pre>",
  ].join("\n"),
};
